                Unlikely, if the powder is low in carbohydrate and the serving is moderate. Gluconeogenesis is driven mainly by the body's need for glucose rather than protein supply, and studies suggest only a modest share of dietary protein ends up as blood glucose. Very large protein meals can lower ketone readings somewhat, so spread protein across the day.
              </p>
